Usage:   sqlr 
Version: 0.3.0

Description:

  Command line for interacting with SQL databases. Use '--help' for each command to list it's parameters

Options:

  -h, --help     - Show this help.                            
  -V, --version  - Show the version number for this program.  
  --debug        - Enable debug logs                          

Commands:

  add-connection                      - Add new connection. Run without parameters to use wizard.           
  rm-connection         [connection]  - Remove selected connection                                          
  get-connection        [connection]  - Get details of selected connection                                  
  get-connection-types                - Get available connection types to be used with '--type' parameter in
                                        'add-connection' command                                            
  connections                         - List all defined connections                                        
  describe                            - Describe all tables and columns available in database               
  query                 [queryArg]    - Run query against specified database                                

",
